==============================================================================
Issue C6-1 — ColumnTransformer silently reorders columns
Source: Rahman et al., printed p.134 (PDF p.141)
==============================================================================

Original input frame:
 Speed  Viscosity  Flowrate
1800.0       25.0    1763.0
2400.0      107.0    1037.0
3000.0      240.0    2247.0
3500.0      520.0    1714.0

Transformer emits columns in this order:
  ['std__Speed', 'std__Flowrate', 'robust__Viscosity']
But the book relabels them as:
  ['Speed', 'Viscosity', 'Flowrate']

--- AS PUBLISHED (mislabelled) ---
    Speed  Viscosity  Flowrate
-1.371758   0.168848 -0.664430
-0.431124  -1.516152 -0.297539
 0.509510   1.292182  0.297539
 1.293372   0.055122  1.550336

--- CORRECTED (labels follow the transformer) ---
    Speed  Viscosity  Flowrate
-1.371758  -0.664430  0.168848
-0.431124  -0.297539 -1.516152
 0.509510   0.297539  1.292182
 1.293372   1.550336  0.055122

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Proof — correlate each labelled column against the true source column:
label       book column tracks     correlation
Speed       Speed                       1.0000   OK
Viscosity   Flowrate                    1.0000   <-- MISLABELLED
Flowrate    Viscosity                   1.0000   <-- MISLABELLED

Book's 'Viscosity' column differs from the true Viscosity: True
Conclusion: 'Viscosity' and 'Flowrate' are transposed in the published code.
